# ==============================================================================
# MealRelay Frontend Environment Configuration Reference
# ==============================================================================
# Usage:
#   Local Dev: Copy this file to `client/.env` (or `client/.env.local`).
#   Production: Configure in your frontend hosting dashboard (e.g., Vercel
#               Project Settings -> Environment Variables).
#
# IMPORTANT SECURITY NOTICE:
#   All variables prefixed with `VITE_` are embedded directly into the public
#   JavaScript bundle at build time. NEVER place database connection strings,
#   JWT secrets, or private server credentials in frontend environment files.
# ==============================================================================

# VITE_API_BASE_URL
# Scope: Frontend (Public / Embedded at Build Time)
# Required: Yes (defaults to 'http://localhost:5000/api' if omitted)
# Controls: The target REST API base endpoint for all frontend HTTP requests.
#           Include the `/api` prefix. Trailing slashes are automatically trimmed.
#
# Examples:
#   Local Development:  http://localhost:5000/api
#   Production (Render): https://your-backend-app.onrender.com/api
#
# Production Location: Vercel Project Settings -> Environment Variables.
#                      Trigger a redeployment whenever this variable is updated.
VITE_API_BASE_URL="http://localhost:5000/api"
